# Source for credential procedure: official Sixteenth-Majles proceedings,
# sessions 2, 25, and 30 (18 February, 18 May, and 1 June 1950).
# The recurring petitions and their effects are counterfactual.
title: Credential Petitions
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: parliamentary_affairs
view-if: credential_petitions_timer <= 0 and majles_convened = 1 and nationalization_approved_majles = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; credential_petitions_timer = 4

= Credential Petitions

Once the {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!} has opened,
a returned deputy is still not automatically a
usable ally. Credentials are considered through parliamentary procedure, and
the {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} must decide
whether to concentrate on documentary case files or on
coordinating interventions in the chamber.

The two methods reinforce different capacities. Neither lets the secretariat
replace the {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!}'s
decisions with its own seat count.

[? if credential_project = "Case-by-case files": The parliamentary group has
already assembled separate files for contested returns. ?]
[? if credential_project = "Floor coordination": Returned opposition deputies
have already divided the speaking work for credential debates. ?]
[? if credential_project_stage > 0: The next petition can deepen that method
or shift attention between documents and the floor. ?]

- @credentials_cases
- @credentials_floor
- @return_card

@credentials_cases
title: Build case-by-case credential files
subtitle: Each disputed return becomes a constitutional case rather than a claim of collective entitlement
on-arrival: {!
Q.credential_project = "Case-by-case files";
Q.credential_project_stage += 1;
var mature = Q.credential_project_stage > 2;
Q.parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += mature ? 2 : 6;
Q.iran_party_organization += mature ? 1 : 3;
for (var place of Q.majles_places) {
    if (place.scenario.contestable &&
        place.scenario.current_return === "returned" &&
        place.scenario.credential !== "approved") {
        place.scenario.legal_defense += mature ? 3 : 10;
        place.scenario.credential_contest = "defended";
    }
}
!}

The committee assembles a separate file for each contested place, preserving
the distinction between a return, an approved credential, and a usable seat.
{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!}
organizers take responsibility for checking the constitutional
argument and its supporting record.

The {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} enters later
debates with better evidence and fewer sweeping claims.
The work is meticulous and does not itself guarantee a favorable vote.
[? if credential_project_stage > 2: The strongest documents are already in
the files. Another review catches omissions and preserves the cases, but
cannot cure a weak return or compel the chamber to approve it. ?]

- @post_event: Continue

@credentials_floor
title: Coordinate floor interventions
subtitle: A disciplined sequence makes the <span class="term term-national-front">Front</span> look like a parliamentary group, not eight unrelated petitioners
on-arrival: {!
Q.credential_project = "Floor coordination";
Q.credential_project_stage += 1;
var mature = Q.credential_project_stage > 2;
Q.oil_coalition_support += mature ? 1 : 2;
Q.independent_nationalists_relation += mature ? 1 : 3;
Q.mossadegh_authority += mature ? 0 : 2;
for (var place of Q.majles_places) {
    if (place.scenario.contestable &&
        place.scenario.current_return === "returned" &&
        place.scenario.credential !== "approved") {
        place.scenario.legal_defense += mature ? 2 : 5;
        place.scenario.credential_contest = "floor coalition";
    }
}
!}

Returned {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} deputies
divide the speaking work and agree on which objections
must be raised together. {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Independent nationalists{!</span>!} gain confidence that their
cases will not disappear behind a single party line.

The coalition looks more purposeful inside the chamber and
{!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mossadegh's{!</span>!}
coordinating authority grows. The documentary basis remains no stronger than
the files already assembled.
[? if credential_project_stage > 2: The deputies already know the order of
speakers and objections. Further coordination prevents mistakes, but produces
little new leverage without stronger cases or additional returned allies. ?]

- @post_event: Continue
